{
  "v": 1,
  "about": "The dynamic network mode's hard denials (docs/adr/0011). A host matches an entry when it is the entry or a name under it; an entry `name.*` matches that label under any public suffix (google.com, google.co.uk). A category denial is refused automatically; the operator may override search, writeup, paste, social and proxy with a reason where the case policy lets them (never under ctf or internal), and never login, upload or credential. An adapter may carry one narrow, declared exception (youtube_oembed: social, title only). Domain categories cannot enforce a published case's integrity alone: a write-up can sit on any personal site, which is why the ctf policy also requires that what is sent is in the evidence.",
